==Latin==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|ine-pro|la}} {{term/t|ine-pro|*gʷerH-||to welcome, greet, praise}}. Cognates include Sanskrit {{term|sc=Deva|गृणाति|tr=gṛṇā́ti||to praise|lang=sa}}, Old Church Slavonic {{term|sc=Cyrs|жрьти|tr=žrĭti||to sacrifice|lang=cu}} and Old Prussian {{term|girtwei||to praise|lang=prg}}.

===Adjective===
{{la-adj-1&2|grātus|grata|grāta|gratum|grātum}}

# [[pleasing]], [[acceptable]], [[agreeable]], [[welcome]]
# [[dear]], [[beloved]]
# [[grateful]], [[thankful]]

====Inflection====
{{la-decl-1&2|grat|grāt}}

* ''comparative'': '''[[gratior|grātior]]''', ''superlative'': '''[[gratissimus|grātissimus]]'''

